    "content": "Gary Woodland underwent successful brain surgery in September 2023 to remove a lesion that was causing severe anxiety and fear. Following his recovery, he was diagnosed with PTSD, yet he returned to the PGA Tour in January 2024 and achieved an emotional victory at the 2026 Houston Open. Key Details Regarding Gary Woodland: The Health Crisis: In 2023, Woodland was diagnosed with a lesion on his brain that was affecting the area controlling fear and anxiety. Surgery: On September 19, 2023, he underwent surgery to remove the tumor. Surgeons had to remove part of the lesion, but left some to prevent potential loss of sight or motor function. Post-Surgery Challenges: Following the surgery, Woodland struggled with intense anxiety, PTSD, and a fear of dying, which significantly impacted his life and game. Return to Golf: He returned to competition in January 2024 but struggled with his game throughout the year, missing 11 of 26 cuts. 2026 Comeback: In March 2026, Woodland opened up about his ongoing battle with PTSD and followed it with an emotional win at the Texas Children’s Houston Open, his first victory since 2019. This video shows Gary Woodland discussing his emotional journey after his win in Houston:54sTenGolfYouTube• Mar 29, 2026 54s Woodland has been widely supported by the golf community and has become a symbol of resilience for others struggling with similar challenges.",
